    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d427">

                <pb facs="0607" n="321" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg321"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 841.857/239</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Germany</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-12-09T17:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 9, 1916, 5 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3651. Department advised that British steamer <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Trevarrick</hi> [<hi rendition="#italic">Trevarrack</hi>], with American
                    citizens on board, was sunk by German <pb facs="0608" n="322" xml:id="pg322"/>
                    submarine 90 miles off Ouessant [Ushant] Point, November 16, and that ship was
                    carrying cargo of grain from Buenos Aires to Hull.</p>
                <p>Request of Foreign Minister prompt investigation and report.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
